WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.473
What the bike will do: on The Class, the rider now reads the plan before they start.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.336
Under the video, one card. The average the bike will ask for, a resistance profile

00:00:15.336 --> 00:00:17.959
of the plan, and the efforts in words.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.821
Nothing here is written by hand. The plan's target power, weighted by time, is two

00:00:28.821 --> 00:00:34.278
hundred and fifty-three point five five watts, shown as about 254. Its seventeen

00:00:34.278 --> 00:00:38.193
efforts run from fifteen seconds to a minute fifteen.

00:00:38.714 --> 00:00:43.959
The profile draws one bar for each of the plan's thirty-three segments: as wide as

00:00:43.959 --> 00:00:49.567
the segment lasts, as tall as its level. A screen reader hears: Resistance profile.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.086
The card from a phone to a desktop. Fitting The Class to one screen is the next

00:00:56.086 --> 00:00:56.725
slice.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.617
The tests came first, and failed. Now one hundred and ninety-one specs and one

00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:10.154
thousand three hundred and sixty-five unit tests pass.

00:01:14.847 --> 00:01:20.501
Telo Ride 1, from the Telo family, is the focused edition of Telo Ride: one class,

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:21.697
nothing else.

00:01:22.042 --> 00:01:26.994
It pairs with a smart bike at home over Bluetooth, plays the class video, or draws

00:01:26.994 --> 00:01:32.006
the Ibiza Sunset Strip course to music if the rider chooses it, and sets the bike's

00:01:32.006 --> 00:01:35.507
resistance for every interval while the rider pedals.

00:01:35.853 --> 00:01:39.828
Connect the bike, take the class, see your number, and come back to beat it.
